A put option (or “put”), which gives the holder the right to sell, can be contrasted with a call option, which provides the holder with the right to buy the underlying security at a specified price, up until the option contract's expiration date. This predetermined price is called the [strike price](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/strikeprice.asp). is relevant
